### TicketFlow - end-to-end demo
### Run the API (`dotnet run --project src/TicketFlow.Api`) and execute the requests top to bottom.
### Works with VS Code "REST Client", JetBrains Rider and Visual Studio 2022+.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5137/api/v1

### 1) Organizer signs in
# @name organizerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "organizer@ticketflow.dev", "password": "Passw0rd!" }

###
@organizerToken = {{organizerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2) Organizer creates a draft event with two tiers
# @name createEvent
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Live Demo Concert",
  "description": "Created from demo.http",
  "venue": "Demo Hall",
  "city": "Istanbul",
  "category": "Concert",
  "startsAt": "2027-03-01T19:00:00+03:00",
  "endsAt": "2027-03-01T22:00:00+03:00",
  "ticketTiers": [
    { "name": "Standard", "price": 500, "capacity": 100 },
    { "name": "Front Row", "price": 1500, "capacity": 2 }
  ]
}

###
@eventId = {{createEvent.response.body.id}}
@frontRowTierId = {{createEvent.response.body.ticketTiers[1].id}}

### 3) Publish it (puts it on sale)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerToken}}

### 4) Anyone can browse the catalogue
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?city=istanbul&sortBy=Price&page=1&pageSize=10

### 5) Customer signs in
# @name customerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "customer@ticketflow.dev", "password": "Passw0rd!" }

###
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 6) Customer reserves both front-row seats (send twice: same Idempotency-Key => same order, 200 + Idempotent-Replayed)
# @name placeOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-order-001

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "items": [ { "ticketTierId": "{{frontRowTierId}}", "quantity": 2 } ] }

###
@orderId = {{placeOrder.response.body.id}}

### 7) The tier is now sold out -> 409 Order.SoldOut
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "items": [ { "ticketTierId": "{{frontRowTierId}}", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### 8) A declined card -> 402 Order.PaymentFailed (reservation is kept)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cardToken": "tok_declined" }

### 9) Pay successfully -> tickets are issued
# @name pay
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cardToken": "tok_visa" }

###
@ticketCode = {{pay.response.body.tickets[0].code}}

### 10) Customer's tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 11) Organizer checks the ticket in at the door (run twice -> 409 Ticket.AlreadyCheckedIn)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/check-in
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{ticketCode}}" }

### 12) Sales report
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/sales-report
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerToken}}

### 13) Refresh-token rotation (run twice: the second call reuses a rotated token -> 401 and all sessions revoked)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### 14) Validation errors are RFC 9457 problem details
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email", "password": "weak", "fullName": "" }

### 15) Health
GET http://localhost:5137/health/ready
